#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184009 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/id #uuid "2cb88713-f830-501e-9b0a-60320936ad14" :question/math-academy-id "e-4792" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\textrm A1] - [\\textrm A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n> *If $\\mathbf{w}$ is a vector such that $\\mathbf{w}+\\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{w}$, then $\\mathbf{w}=\\mathbf{0}$.*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}w + w|= w & [given] \\\\ (w + w) + (-w)|= w + (-w) & [add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides] \\\\ w + (w + (-w))|= w + (-w) & [axiom __] \\\\ w + 0|= 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ w|= 0 & [axiom __]\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe axioms:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}[A1]: x + y = y + x & [A5]: 1 \\cdot x = x \\\\ [A2]: (x + y) + z = x + (y + z) & [A6]: α(βx) = (αβ)x \\\\ [A3]: x + 0 = x & [A7]: (α + β)x = αx + βx \\\\ [A4]: x + (-x) = 0 & [A8]: α(x + y) = αx + αy\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Using the axioms of a vector space, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}w + w &= w & [given] \\\\ (w + w) + (-w)|= w + (-w) & [add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides] \\\\ w + (w + (-w))|= w + (-w) & [axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A2}}[/math]] \\\\ w + 0|= 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ w|= 0 & [axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A3}}[/math]]\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184038 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/id #uuid "132efc65-5f50-5582-8955-a5d34c57af04" :question/math-academy-id "e-8224" :question/problem "Let $V$ be the set of all real polynomials of degree exactly $3$, equipped with the usual addition and scalar multiplication operations. Complete the following sentence:\n\n> *$V$ is **not** a vector space because $\\textrm{_________}\\,$.*\n\n1. the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$\n2. $V$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) \\in V$\n3. addition of polynomials is not commutative" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n> *$V$ is **not** a vector space because **the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$.***\n\nFor instance, if\n\n$$\np(x) = 1 +x^3\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nq(x) = 1-x^3\n$$\n\n, then $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are in $V$. However\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np(x) + q(x) &= (1 + x^{3}) + (1 - x^{3}) \\\\\n&= 2 ∉ V\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative.\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $3$, the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ also has degree $3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2420a1a1-dd4c-5f7d-a312-35a9e5cf4e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183108} {:answer/id #uuid "51577410-6160-522c-9205-9abb45526d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) ∈ W$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183109} {:answer/id #uuid "67cc8a1f-d027-5d95-bb4f-e91b729b3fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183110} {:answer/id #uuid "76898a5b-5be3-5841-8a7a-1f8e1195ab1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183111} {:answer/id #uuid "78561a3b-a374-507a-8dc2-675e93cda539" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67cc8a1f-d027-5d95-bb4f-e91b729b3fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183110} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a983190-e5b4-581c-80c6-c9780ac1d1ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183107}] :question/id #uuid "ac2c9af3-5c5a-5bc3-898a-7e78bc1b3b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35558" :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x ∈ R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n> *$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $_________$.*"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e9f84ab-a18d-5daa-92af-3bfafebcac8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A8$, $A4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183114} {:answer/id #uuid "a101de1b-85e7-5397-97ac-e463b9762fce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A7$, $A3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183115} {:answer/id #uuid "f877952c-54a0-51e5-85be-a003422f2c56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A6$, $A4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183116} {:answer/id #uuid "13147798-07ba-57bf-9a84-6677faf63280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A6$, $A3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183117} {:answer/id #uuid "159fee67-2f63-5af5-ba27-7e53c67c8b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A8$, $A3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "159fee67-2f63-5af5-ba27-7e53c67c8b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A8$, $A3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183118} :answer-field/id #uuid "9386a449-908e-5720-a9a3-83c55527b4f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183113}] :question/id #uuid "45dd4a34-5d24-5e1b-9442-ff816cade184" :question/math-academy-id "q-35583" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[A1] - [A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n> *$α0 = 0$ for any $α ∈ R$*\n\n*Proof:*\n$\\begin{bmatrix}α0|= α0 & [given] \\\\ α0|= α(0 + 0) & [axiom A3] \\\\ α0|= α0 + α0 & [axiom __] \\\\ α0 + (- α0)|= (α0 + α0) + (- α0) & [add- α0to both sides] \\\\ α0 + (- α0)|= α0 + (α0 + (- α0)) & [axiom A2] \\\\ 0|= α0 + 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ 0|= α0 & [axiom __]\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe axioms:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}[A1]: x + y = y + x & [A5]: 1 \\cdot x = x \\\\ [A2]: (x + y) + z = x + (y + z) & [A6]: α(βx) = (αβ)x \\\\ [A3]: x + 0 = x & [A7]: (α + β)x = αx + βx \\\\ [A4]: x + (-x) = 0 & [A8]: α(x + y) = αx + αy\\end{bmatrix}$"}]}
